   "id": "f-bl-1",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Bleakspire is a fortress with a small city around it, on a large island. About 4,000 people live inside the walls and about 1,500 outside them. The walls were built for about 14,000, so most buildings stand empty.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-020; R-068; R-076; R-105"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": "Violent storms, hard winters, and walls built for far more of us than there are.",
   "id": "f-bl-2",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "It sits on a coastal inlet, with valleys behind the headland for farms and timber. The storms are violent and the winters are harsh.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-068; R-105"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-bl-3",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "The city has seven wards inside the walls (Fortress, Hall Square, {{harbour|the Harbour}}, Manor Ward, Market Ward, Old Town and {{hollows|the Hollows}}) plus the Outer Ring. The Mayor governs with a small cadre of high elven bureaucrats.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-070; R-037"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-bl-4",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 10,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Fishing feeds about half the city. Three walled farms still work the hinterland, all held by {{greenmantle|House Greenmantle}}. Most of the outer farms were overrun long ago.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-069; R-077; R-082"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-bl-5",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 12,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Port Dawnreach is a much larger city on another landmass. It is Bleakspire's long-haul sea link and trading partner, not a nearby port.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-068 (CX-093)"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-bl-6",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 15,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "How old the walls are, and who built them.",
   "body": "Bleakspire began as a Tyraniff Empire research fortress for weapons and magitech, built roughly 1,000 to 1,200 years ago and meant to sit out of the way. When the empire fell, the supply ships stopped and the city had to learn to feed itself.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-069"
  },
  {
   "skill": "alchemy",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": "What scavenged magical technology is and who buys it is magic/engineering knowledge.",
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-bl-7",
   "entry_id": "bleakspire",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 18,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "What people have scavenged over the years, and who would take it.",
   "body": "Over time, people here have scavenged magical technology without knowing what it did. They could trade it to the Alchemists, and to merchants who traded with the Alchemists.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-105 (TC-700 B2)"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-ho-1",
   "entry_id": "hollows",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "The Hollows are the most abandoned ward in {{bleakspire|Bleakspire}}. The great majority of the buildings are empty, degraded or ruined, and gardens grow inside the shells.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
