   "id": "f-ha-1",
   "entry_id": "harbour",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "The Harbour is the second most abandoned ward. Well under half of it is in use. A couple of quays still work, and the shipyard is ruined.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-106"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-ha-2",
   "entry_id": "harbour",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Fishing is about half of what {{bleakspire|Bleakspire}} eats, so the small boats on the beach and the inlet matter more than they look.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-069"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-ha-3",
   "entry_id": "harbour",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 10,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Lockjaw, an orc and a former Alchemist marine, is the Docksmaster. {{the-empress|The Empress}} is the flagship of the harbour, and Salt captains her.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B4; R-019; R-023"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": "Fix a quay before there is a breakwater, and the next storm takes it back.",
   "id": "f-ha-4",
   "entry_id": "harbour",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 14,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "Why the quays keep breaking.",
   "body": "Storms undo repaired quays. Until there is a breakwater, any quay that gets restored is at risk every time the weather turns.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-110"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-hh-1",
   "entry_id": "hills-hearth",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Hill's Hearth is a bar in {{bleakspire|Bleakspire}}. Folk call it a drow loyalist bar. Which ward it stands in: [TBD].",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B4"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-hh-2",
   "entry_id": "hills-hearth",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 12,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "The story goes that a drow house split, and the Imperial Loyalists went underground.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B4"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-co-1",
   "entry_id": "company",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "The party that deposed and killed the Emperor named themselves the Empire Mercenary Company ({{emperors-fall|the Emperor's fall}}). {{valthar|Valthar Brightlance}} leads it.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B3; R-115"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": "Forty to sixty of us, and a great deal of wall.",
   "id": "f-co-2",
   "entry_id": "company",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "It is a Company, not a guild, though it works like one: members pool their resources to get assignments done. At {{bleakspire|Bleakspire}} it is a thin cadre of about 40 to 60, and holding the walls is a real problem.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-040; R-070"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-co-3",
   "entry_id": "company",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 12,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "There are seven officers: Alexandria, {{aligher|Aligher}}, David, Earl, Gorbon, Jadross and {{valthar|Valthar}}, who leads them. All seven were the party that brought down the Emperor.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-116; R-117"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-co-4",
   "entry_id": "company",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 10,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Loot is split 40% to you, 40% to your squad and 20% to the Company purse. City rebuilds are paid from the Company or squad purse.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-072; R-110"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-co-5",
   "entry_id": "company",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 15,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "Why Valthar runs it the way he does.",
   "body": "Valthar holds the clearance for the high-level adventuring contracts. He calls it a company because he is a military man and sees it as a paramilitary outfit.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-035; R-040"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-gm-1",
   "entry_id": "greenmantle",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "House Greenmantle is a wood-elf house. It holds most of the natural-resource work outside the walls of {{bleakspire|Bleakspire}}: timber, farming and hunting. Its main estate is outside the walls; it keeps a town lodge in Manor Ward.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B4; R-070; R-071"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-gm-2",
   "entry_id": "greenmantle",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "It owns all three working walled farms: Pine Apple Press Farm, Tepeyac Ranch, and Root and Runner, which is the farthest out and the most heavily guarded.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-077; R-082"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": "The Dude doesn't seem to care who runs things. \"Seem\" is the word we keep using.",
   "id": "f-gm-3",
   "entry_id": "greenmantle",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 12,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "The head of the house is Lord Greenmantle, called \"The Dude\". He has no other name. He is easy-going and doesn't seem interested in running things, at least as far as we have learned. It could be an act. His niece is Stella.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B4; R-019"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-gm-4",
   "entry_id": "greenmantle",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 15,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "What became of the son who ran the timber.",
   "body": "His elder son, Thananir, ran the timber. Thananir is dead.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "TC-700 B4"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-va-1",
   "entry_id": "valthar",
   "tier": "common",
   "dc": null,
   "dc_is_placeholder": false,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "Valthar Brightlance leads {{company|the Company}}. He led the party of seven that deposed and killed the Emperor ({{emperors-fall|the Emperor's fall}}).",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-035; R-117"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": "He never asked anyone to follow him. They followed anyway.",
   "id": "f-va-2",
   "entry_id": "valthar",
   "tier": "baseline",
   "dc": 10,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": null,
   "body": "He never came out and said he was the leader. He recruited the people, and the party looked to him. He is one of the seven officers.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-035; R-116"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-va-3",
   "entry_id": "valthar",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 15,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "Where he came from, before any of this.",
   "body": "He started as a farmer, called to war by his liegelord: border skirmishes between lords on another continent. He rose through the ranks as a natural leader. When he went home, his family farm was burned and his village razed.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-026"
  },
  {
   "skill": "history",
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
   "id": "f-va-4",
   "entry_id": "valthar",
   "tier": "roll",
   "dc": 18,
   "dc_is_placeholder": true,
   "teaser": "Who trained him, and what he did after.",
   "body": "With no ties left, he took the Alchemists' offer and trained as an Inquisitor. He was of low birth, not high enough for their knightly orders. Later he led a team of his own on missions recovering magical items.",
   "adds_aliases": [],
   "editorial_status": "canon",
   "canon_ref": "R-026"
  },
  {
   "skill": null,
   "culture_id": null,
   "skill_tag_reason": null,
   "pull_quote": null,
